# Musician Expense Tracker — Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
Discord bot for a musician/music teacher to track income & expenses via photos, text,
and audio messages. Uses Gemini 3 Flash for data extraction, Google Sheets for storage.
High-confidence entries are auto-saved; low-confidence entries prompt for clarification.

## Architecture Awareness
- `main.py` — Discord bot, event handlers, auto-confirm flow, commands. Entry point.
- `gemini_processor.py` — Gemini API calls. Uses `google-genai` SDK (NOT `google-generativeai`).
- `sheets_manager.py` — Google Sheets via `gspread`. Two tabs: "Entries" + "Conversation Log".
  Sync library wrapped in `asyncio.to_thread()`.
- `prompts.py` — System prompts AND Pydantic response models. These are tightly coupled.
- `config.py` — Env var loading. Handles full Sheet URLs automatically.

## Spreadsheet Schema
Entries tab columns: Date, Type, Category, Client/Event, Vendor, Mode of Payment,
Amount ($), Description, Notes, Discord Link, Timestamp.

Categories:
- Income: Teaching, Performance
- Expense: IT, Performance, Teaching

Client/Event and Mode of Payment are income-only. Vendor is expense-only.

## Coding Conventions
- Python 3.11+ with type hints on all functions.
- Async/await for all I/O operations. The Discord bot loop is async.
- Use `logging` module, never `print()`.
- Handle exceptions in Discord event handlers — never let them crash the bot.
  Report errors to the user in the Discord thread.
- Keep imports sorted: stdlib → third-party → local.

## Key Libraries
- `discord.py` — Discord bot framework. Use `commands.Bot`, not raw `Client`.
- `google-genai` — Gemini API. Use `client.aio.models.generate_content()` for async.
  Use `types.Part.from_bytes()` for inline image/audio data.
  Use `response_schema=PydanticModel` for structured JSON output.
- `gspread` — Google Sheets. Synchronous — always wrap in `asyncio.to_thread()`.

## Emoji Reactions
- Hourglass: processing
- Green checkmark: saved to sheet
- Speech bubble: waiting for user clarification
- Red X: actual error only (never for "needs input")

## Important Reminders
- When changing the Pydantic models in `prompts.py`, also update the system prompt text
  to match (they must stay in sync about categories, field meanings, etc.).
- When changing the Google Sheet columns, update BOTH `sheets_manager.HEADERS` and
  `sheets_manager.append_entry()`.
- After any architectural change, UPDATE `AGENTS.md` in the project root.
- Confidence is based on structured fields only (Date through Amount).
  Description and Notes are best-effort and never lower confidence.
- The bot uses in-memory `pending_entries` dict — entries are lost on restart.
  This is acceptable for an MVP but should be noted.
